\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. As helpless as a child who clings 
\par Fast to his father's arm,
\par And casts His weakness on the strength
\par That keeps him safe from harm:
\par So I, my Father, cling to Thee,
\par And thus I every hour 
\par Would link my earthly feebleness
\par To Thine almighty power.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. As trustful as a child who looks
\par Up in his mother's face,
\par And all his little griefs and fears
\par Forgets in her embrace:
\par So I to Thee, my Saviour, look,
\par And in Thy face divine
\par Can read the love that will sustain
\par as weak a faith as mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. As loving as a child who sits
\par Close by his parent's knee,
\par And knows no want while he have
\par That sweet society:
\par So sitting at thy feet, my heart
\par Would all its love outpour,
\par And  pray that Thou wouldst teach me, Lord,
\par To love Thee more and more.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

